{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ml-explore/mlx/pulls/3828","id":4027558207,"node_id":"PR_kwDOKzRn187wD6k_","html_url":"https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx/pull/3828","diff_url":"https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx/pull/3828.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx/pull/3828.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ml-explore/mlx/issues/3828","number":3828,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix captured random state in compile","user":{"login":"angeloskath","id":1242043,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNDIwNDM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1242043?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/angeloskath","html_url":"https://github.com/angeloskath","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angeloskath/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angeloskath/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angeloskath/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angeloskath/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angeloskath/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angeloskath/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angeloskath/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angeloskath/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angeloskath/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This is an interesting bug. In our attempts at thread-safety, compile now captures the random state of the thread that created the function and not the thread that called the function which can (and often is) different.\r\n\r\nThere isn't too clean of a solution that I could think of so please be as strict as possible in your judgment. The current approach is twofold\r\n\r\n1. Make the random state a singleton object that fetches the thread local state. This makes it ok to capture on any thread. Accessing its one element will get you the correct array based on which thread you are on.\r\n2. The ugly part of this fix is that `tree_visit` and `tree_visit_update` now have a special case where if they encounter a random state they instead operate on the underlying array. This is ugly because it is not necessarily consistent with `tree_map` or multi-tree `tree_visit`.\r\n\r\nThis closes https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx-lm/pull/1444 and fixes https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx-lm/issues/1439 .","created_at":"2026-07-10T07:17:25Z","updated_at":"2026-07-20T20:09:35Z","closed_at":"2026-07-20T20:09:33Z","merged_at":"2026-07-20T20:09:33Z","merge_commit_sha":"ce3073389e92d8f7b7ecd3d7697523795786e046","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ml-explore/mlx/pulls/3828/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ml-explore/mlx/pulls/3828/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ml-explore/mlx/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ml-explore/mlx/issues/3828/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ml-explore/mlx/statuses/f50d146367c18f822d565c4d61ed053cf0179d44","head":{"label":"ml-explore:fix-compile-random-state","ref":"fix-compile-random-state","sha":"f50d146367c18f822d565c4d61ed053cf0179d44","user":{"login":"ml-explore","id":102832242,"node_id":"O_kgDOBiEYcg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102832242?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ml-explore","html_url":"https://github.com/ml-explore","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ml-explore/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ml-explore/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ml-explore/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ml-explore/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ml-explore/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.